Fictional EP Tracklist

Track 1: Step-On-No-Tile-Seams
- Story & Context: Recorded during the ship's initial engine-flip sequence near the midpoint of the voyage, this opening track captures the exact moment the crew lost radio contact with Earth, turning anxiety into a game of childhood balance. Marimbist Hideo Vance composed the main motif by assigning specific notes to the metal floor plates of the hydroponics bay while stepping over their magnetic seals. During the live tracking session, a hydraulic leak caused a soft hissing sound that was kept in the final mix, perfectly matching the muted flugelhorn’s entrance. The song launched the Starlight Bossa-Cool movement when it was broadcast across the ship's internal PA network. "If you touch the brass line, you fall straight through the floor," whispers the soft vocal hook over a gentle 5/4 marimba roll.
