Track 2: Derelict-Hop
- Story & Context: A character study of Chief Engineer Samira Lin, who spent her off-duty hours sneaking into the ship's silent cargo holds to dance to shortwave radio static. The title uses local deck-slang for the light-headed, low-gravity shuffle step the crew invented to conserve energy during power-rationing cycles. Lin contributed her own vocals via a suit-comm microphone, creating a dry, intimate counterpoint to the cascading marimba arpeggios. The session was interrupted when an unmapped micro-meteorite struck the outer hull, adding an accidental, perfectly timed metallic thud to the track's quiet bridge. "We step real light so the sensor doesn't know we're gone," sings Lin over a hushed, walking gut-string bass.
